 "about": "Xiegu's X6100 base V1.1.9 (251127001) with GoldCorpHF's fixes: the codec's PLL fraction written as Xiegu meant it (the I/Q rate 100 kHz, not 99,932 Hz), no +6 dB on the TX power loop from 29.7 MHz up, the TX power loop's floor -60 dB, not -40 (0.1 W reached on every band; 6 m gave 0.8 W, HF 0.2-0.3), the TX power loop held while the transmitter is silent (no burst of drive on the first sound after a pause; Xiegu's gave 1.0 W at a 0.1 W setting), the transmitter's I/Q balance set per band by the GUI through register 52 (the other sideband's image, -42 to -54 dBc on every X6100 base, cancelled by a calibration), the TX DC offsets the GUI sends kept through band changes (Xiegu's base loaded its own table's, zeros, over them: the carrier back after each band change)",
